{"name":"Shadow Play","hex":"#2d1403","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shadow play","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ancient form of storytelling and entertainment using opaque, often articulated figures in front of an illuminated backdrop to create the illusion of moving images.","A play of this form."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow_play"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shadow play","blocks":[{"text":"Shadow play, also known as shadow puppetry, is an ancient form of storytelling and entertainment which uses flat articulated cut-out figures which are held between a source of light and a translucent screen or scrim. The cut-out shapes of the puppets sometimes include translucent color or other types of detailing. Various effects can be achieved by moving both the puppets and the light source. A skilled puppeteer can make the figures appear to walk, dance, fight, nod and laugh."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg/330px-Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_play"},{"title":"Shadow Play (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Shadow Play is a world-record-holding standardbred racehorse. He was sired by The Panderosa, out of Matts Filly, a Matts Scooter mare. The colt was purchased as a yearling for $16,000, and is owned by Dr Ian Moore of Charlottetown, PEI, R G McGroup LTD of Bathurst, NB, and Hockey Hall of Fame inductee Serge Savard of Saint-Bruno-de-Montarville, Quebec. In 2022, Shadow Play was inducted into the Canadian Horse Racing Hall of Fame."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_Play_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg/500px-Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg/1280px-Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg/500px-Ki_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A performance of wayang, an Indonesian shadow puppet form","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKi_Sigit_Ariyanto_Dalang_Wayang_Kulit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/OFB-Qianlongsatz03-Krieger.JPG/500px-OFB-Qianlongsatz03-Krieger.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/OFB-Qianlongsatz03-Krieger.JPG/1280px-OFB-Qianlongsatz03-Krieger.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/OFB-Qianlongsatz03-Krieger.JPG/500px-OFB-Qianlongsatz03-Krieger.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOFB-Qianlongsatz03-Krieger.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/The_Childrens_Museum_of_Indianapolis_-_Han_shadow_puppet.jpg/500px-The_Childrens_Museum_of_Indianapolis_-_Han_shadow_puppet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/The_Childrens_Museum_of_Indianapolis_-_Han_shadow_puppet.jpg/500px-The_Childrens_Museum_of_Indianapolis_-_Han_shadow_puppet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This Chinese shadow puppet is illustrative of the ornate detail that goes into the figures. From the collection of The Children's Museum of Indianapolis.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Childrens_Museum_of_Indianapolis_-_Han_shadow_puppet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Chinese_shadow_puppetry.jpg/500px-Chinese_shadow_puppetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Chinese_shadow_puppetry.jpg/500px-Chinese_shadow_puppetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chinese shadow puppetry is a form of theater whereby colorful silhouette figures perform traditional plays against a back-lit cloth screen, accompanied by music. From Kaifeng Prefecture.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChinese_shadow_puppetry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Greek_Shadow_Puppetry.jpg/500px-Greek_Shadow_Puppetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Greek_Shadow_Puppetry.jpg/1280px-Greek_Shadow_Puppetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Greek_Shadow_Puppetry.jpg/500px-Greek_Shadow_Puppetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example of shadow puppetry in Greece","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreek_Shadow_Puppetry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Th%C3%A9atre_d%27Ombres_in_Le_Chat_Noir.jpg/500px-Th%C3%A9atre_d%27Ombres_in_Le_Chat_Noir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Th%C3%A9atre_d%27Ombres_in_Le_Chat_Noir.jpg/500px-Th%C3%A9atre_d%27Ombres_in_Le_Chat_Noir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stagehands moving zinc figures behind the screen of the Théatre d'Ombres in Le Chat Noir","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATh%C3%A9atre_d'Ombres_in_Le_Chat_Noir.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Ombra_francese_seconda.jpg/500px-Ombra_francese_seconda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Ombra_francese_seconda.jpg/500px-Ombra_francese_seconda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Part of the collection of the Museo del Precinema, Padua, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOmbra_francese_seconda.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Hanuman_and_Ravana_in_Tholu_Bommalata%2C_the_shadow_puppet_tradition_of_Andhra_Pradesh%2C_India.JPG/500px-Hanuman_and_Ravana_in_Tholu_Bommalata%2C_the_shadow_puppet_tradition_of_Andhra_Pradesh%2C_India.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Hanuman_and_Ravana_in_Tholu_Bommalata%2C_the_shadow_puppet_tradition_of_Andhra_Pradesh%2C_India.JPG/1280px-Hanuman_and_Ravana_in_Tholu_Bommalata%2C_the_shadow_puppet_tradition_of_Andhra_Pradesh%2C_India.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Hanuman_and_Ravana_in_Tholu_Bommalata%2C_the_shadow_puppet_tradition_of_Andhra_Pradesh%2C_India.JPG/500px-Hanuman_and_Ravana_in_Tholu_Bommalata%2C_the_shadow_puppet_tradition_of_Andhra_Pradesh%2C_India.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hanuman and Ravana in tholu bommalata, the shadow puppet tradition of Andhra Pradesh, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHanuman_and_Ravana_in_Tholu_Bommalata%2C_the_shadow_puppet_tradition_of_Andhra_Pradesh%2C_India.JPG"}],"sounds":{}}}